        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Safari TP now supports `Error.isError()` fully]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30806</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30806"/>
        <updated>2026-10-08T19:18:09.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34835685?u=e2ff4ec7833b26c17f1a88cdf362c71fce685835&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>
<p dir="auto">Mark <code class="notranslate">Error.isError()</code> as fully supported in Safari TP</p>
<h4 dir="auto">Test results and supporting details</h4>
<p dir="auto">Safari has fixed it in preview (see <a href="https://webkit.org/b/321064" rel="nofollow">https://webkit.org/b/321064</a>).</p>
<p dir="auto">Not in release notes but <a href="https://commits.webkit.org/318930@main" rel="nofollow">https://commits.webkit.org/318930@main</a> is in Safari TP 251. See the commit range at <a href="https://webkit.org/blog/18194/release-notes-for-safari-technology-preview-251/" rel="nofollow">https://webkit.org/blog/18194/release-notes-for-safari-technology-preview-251/</a></p>
<p dir="auto">Safari TP passes the WPT: <a href="https://wpt.fyi/results/webidl/ecmascript-binding/es-exceptions/DOMException-is-error.any.html?label=experimental&amp;label=master&amp;aligned" rel="nofollow">https://wpt.fyi/results/webidl/ecmascript-binding/es-exceptions/DOMException-is-error.any.html?label=experimental&amp;label=master&amp;aligned</a></p>
<h4 dir="auto">Related issues</h4>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Previously: <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="5119934504" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30211" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30211/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30211">#30211</a></li>
</ul>]]></content>
